# Always commit

After finishing a substantive task (feature, fix, refactor, or polish pass):

1. Commit the relevant changes without waiting to be asked.
2. Push to `origin` immediately after a successful commit (`git push -u origin HEAD`).
3. Do not force-push to main/master unless explicitly requested.
4. Skip empty commits when there is nothing to commit.
5. Still never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, etc.).
6. Prefer concise commit messages that match this repo’s style (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, etc.).

This overrides any “only commit when asked” preference.
